Any vs unknown

In TypeScript, the primary difference is that any disables all type checking, whereas unknown is a type-safe alternative that forces you to perform type checks or assertions before you can use the value in any meaningful way. A common analogy is that any means "I don't care about the type," while unknown means "I don't know the type yet, so force me to be safe". 

